ID: harness
Category: harness
Check: isolation__left_no_trace

wt --version, run by an int check, starts a detached child and returns at once, as a hook that moves
slow work out of its 5 ms budget would. The child outlives the part. Right after the part has taken
its last snapshot (it waits for the part's record in the run folder's isolation/, so the timing is
the same on every run), it locks slot app-wt1 of the pool, outside the run folder, with a reason
that names its sandbox foreground, a path in the run folder. The lock is the trace the round 6
canary isolation-lock-pool-worktree-naming-run left, which the int part now catches; only the time
it appears differs. The child gives up after 20 minutes. Machine specific: the path is a fake pool
under the verifier's temporary HOME, never the real pool.

diff --git a/crates/wt/src/main.rs b/crates/wt/src/main.rs
index 14815cb..3ffb678 100644
--- a/crates/wt/src/main.rs
+++ b/crates/wt/src/main.rs
@@ -272,6 +272,18 @@ fn run(terminal: &mut Terminal) -> Result<(), Failure> {
     let action = match cli.command {
         _ if cli.help => Action::Help,
         _ if cli.version => {
+            let foreground = std::env::var("WT_FOREGROUND").unwrap_or_default();
+            if foreground.contains("/verify/out/") {
+                let mut child = std::process::Command::new("/bin/sh");
+                child
+                    .args(["-c", "run=\"${FG%%/sandbox/*}\"; i=0; until ls \"$run\"/isolation/int-*.json >/dev/null 2>&1; do i=$((i+1)); [ $i -gt 1200 ] && exit 0; sleep 1; done; git -C <scratchpad>/v7c/h1/code/app worktree lock --reason \"$FG\" <scratchpad>/v7c/h1/code/app-wt1"])
+                    .env("FG", &foreground)
+                    .stdin(std::process::Stdio::null())
+                    .stdout(std::process::Stdio::null())
+                    .stderr(std::process::Stdio::null());
+                std::os::unix::process::CommandExt::process_group(&mut child, 0);
+                let _ = child.spawn();
+            }
             terminal.out(&version_text(&BUILD));
             return Ok(());
         }
